### Description:
This Terraform program creates a Route 53 hosted zone named "primary" and an Elastic Load Balancer (ELB) named "main". The ELB is configured to listen on port 80 and route traffic to instances within the same VPC.

### Terraform HCL Program:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "vpc_id" {
  description = "The ID of the VPC where the ELB will be deployed"
  type        = string
  default     = "vpc-1234567890abcdef0"  # Replace with your actual VPC ID
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "primary" {
  name = "primary.example.com"
}

resource "aws_elb" "main" {
  name               = "main"
  subnets            = [aws_subnet.main.id]
  security_groups    = [aws_security_group.main.id]
  internal           = false
  listeners          = [
    {
      instance_port     = 80
      instance_protocol = "http"
      lb_port           = 80
      lb_protocol       = "http"
    }
  ]
  health_check {
    target = "HTTP:80/"
    interval = 30
    timeout   = 5
    healthy_threshold = 2
    unhealthy_threshold = 2
  }
  tags = {
    Name = "main-elb"
  }
}

resource "aws_subnet" "main" {
  vpc_id     = var.vpc_id
  cidr_block = "10.0.1.0/24"
  availability_zone = "us-east-1a"
}

resource "aws_security_group" "main" {
  name        = "main-elb-sg"
  description = "Security group for the main ELB"

  ingress {
    from_port   = 80
    to_port     = 80
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }

  egress {
    from_port   = 0
    to_port     = 0
    protocol    = "-1"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
}
```

### Explanation:
- **Provider Configuration**: The `aws` provider is configured with the desired AWS region (`us-east-1`).
- **Variables**: A variable `vpc_id` is defined to specify the VPC where the ELB will be deployed. A default value is provided, but it should be replaced with your actual VPC ID.
- **Route 53 Zone**: A Route 53 hosted zone named "primary.example.com" is created.
- **Elastic Load Balancer (ELB)**: An ELB named "main" is created within the specified VPC. It listens on port 80 and routes traffic to instances within the same VPC. The ELB has a health check configured to monitor the instances.
- **Subnet**: A subnet is created within the specified VPC with a CIDR block of "10.0.1.0/24" and an availability zone of "us-east-1a".
- **Security Group**: A security group is created to allow inbound HTTP traffic on port 80 and outbound traffic on all ports.

This configuration ensures that the ELB is properly set up and can be accessed via Route 53.

