### Description:
This Terraform program defines a basic Amazon Kendra index resource along with a user group resolution configuration. The index will be created in the specified AWS region, and the user group resolution configuration will allow Kendra to resolve user groups based on their email addresses.

### Terraform HCL Program:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "kendra_index_name" {
  description = "The name of the Kendra index"
  default     = "MyKendraIndex"
}

variable "kendra_user_group_resolution_config" {
  description = "Configuration for user group resolution"
  type        = object({
    user_group_resolution_mode = string
    user_group_index_field = string
  })
  default = {
    user_group_resolution_mode = "Email"
    user_group_index_field = "email"
  }
}

resource "aws_kendra_index" "example" {
  name = var.kendra_index_name

  user_group_resolution_configuration {
    user_group_resolution_mode = var.kendra_user_group_resolution_config.user_group_resolution_mode
    user_group_index_field      = var.kendra_user_group_resolution_config.user_group_index_field
  }
}
```

### Explanation:
- **Provider Configuration**: The `aws` provider is configured with the desired AWS region (`us-west-2` in this example).
- **Variables**:
  - `kendra_index_name`: A variable to specify the name of the Kendra index. It defaults to "MyKendraIndex".
  - `kendra_user_group_resolution_config`: A variable to configure the user group resolution settings. It includes:
    - `user_group_resolution_mode`: Specifies how Kendra resolves user groups. Options include "Email", "IAMRole", and "Custom". Defaults to "Email".
    - `user_group_index_field`: The field in the index that contains the user group information. Defaults to "email".
- **Resource**: The `aws_kendra_index` resource is defined with the specified name and user group resolution configuration.

