### Description of the Terraform Program

This Terraform script will configure an OpenID Connect (OIDC) identity provider for an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS) cluster named "example". The script will create the necessary IAM roles and policies, and set up the OIDC configuration for the EKS cluster.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "cluster_name" {
  default = "example"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "eks_oidc_role" {
  name = "${var.cluster_name}-oidc-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Federated = "arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:oidc-provider/${var.cluster_name}.eks.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Condition = {
          StringEquals = {
            "oidc.eks.amazonaws.com:sub": "system:serviceaccount:${var.cluster_name}:default"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "eks_oidc_policy_attachment" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.eks_oidc_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKSClusterPolicy"
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "eks_oidc_policy_attachment_2" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.eks_oidc_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKSServicePolicy"
}

resource "aws_eks_cluster" "example" {
  name     = var.cluster_name
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.eks_oidc_role.arn

  vpc_config {
    subnet_ids = ["subnet-12345678", "subnet-23456789"]  # Replace with your subnet IDs
  }

  oidc_config {
    issuer_url = "https://oidc.eks.${data.aws_region.current.name}.amazonaws.com/id/${var.cluster_name}"
    client_id  = "sts.amazonaws.com"
  }
}

data "aws_caller_identity" "current" {}

data "aws_region" "current" {}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The `provider "aws"` block specifies the AWS region where the resources will be created.

2. **Variables**: The `variable "cluster_name"` is defined with a default value of "example".

3. **IAM Role**: 
   - `aws_iam_role` creates an IAM role named `${var.cluster_name}-oidc-role`.
   - The `assume_role_policy` allows the EKS service account to assume this role using the OIDC provider.

4. **IAM Policy Attachments**:
   - Two policy attachments are added to the role: `AmazonEKSClusterPolicy` and `AmazonEKSServicePolicy`.

5. **EKS Cluster**:
   - `aws_eks_cluster` creates the EKS cluster named `${var.cluster_name}`.
   - The `role_arn` is set to the IAM role created above.
   - `vpc_config` specifies the subnet IDs for the VPC where the cluster will be deployed.
   - `oidc_config` sets up the OIDC configuration with the issuer URL and client ID.

6. **Data Sources**:
   - `data "aws_caller_identity" "current"` retrieves the current AWS account ID.
   - `data "aws_region" "current"` retrieves the current AWS region.

This script assumes you have the necessary permissions to create IAM roles, policies, and EKS clusters in the specified AWS region. Adjust the subnet IDs and other configurations as needed for your environment.

