### Description:
This Terraform program creates an Amazon DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster using the `aws_dax_cluster` resource. The cluster will have a node type of `dax.r4.large` and a replication factor of 1, meaning it will consist of a single node.

### Terraform HCL Program:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "cluster_name" {
  default = "my-dax-cluster"
}

resource "aws_dax_cluster" "example" {
  cluster_name           = var.cluster_name
  node_type              = "dax.r4.large"
  replication_factor    = 1
  subnet_group_name      = aws_subnet_group.example.name
  security_group_ids     = [aws_security_group.example.id]
  iam_role_arns          = [aws_iam_role.dax_role.arn]

  tags = {
    Name = var.cluster_name
  }
}

resource "aws_subnet_group" "example" {
  name       = var.cluster_name
  description = "Subnet group for DAX cluster"

  subnet_ids = [
    aws_subnet.public_subnet_1.id,
    aws_subnet.public_subnet_2.id,
    aws_subnet.public_subnet_3.id,
  ]
}

resource "aws_security_group" "example" {
  name        = var.cluster_name
  description = "Security group for DAX cluster"

  ingress {
    from_port   = 9100
    to_port     = 9100
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }

  egress {
    from_port   = 0
    to_port     = 0
    protocol    = "-1"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "dax_role" {
  name = var.cluster_name

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "dax.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "dax_policy_attachment" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.dax_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSAmazonDAXServiceRole"
}
```

### Explanation:
- **Provider Configuration**: The `aws` provider is configured with the desired AWS region (`us-west-2`).
- **Variables**: A variable `cluster_name` is defined with a default value of `my-dax-cluster`.
- **DAX Cluster**: The `aws_dax_cluster` resource is created with the specified node type (`dax.r4.large`), replication factor (`1`), subnet group name, security group IDs, and IAM role ARN.
- **Subnet Group**: The `aws_subnet_group` resource defines the subnets where the DAX nodes will be deployed.
- **Security Group**: The `aws_security_group` resource allows inbound traffic on port 9100 (the DAX port) and outbound traffic on all ports.
- **IAM Role**: The `aws_iam_role` resource is created to allow the DAX service to assume the role.
- **IAM Policy Attachment**: The `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment` resource attaches the AWSAmazonDAXServiceRole policy to the DAX role.

This configuration ensures that the DAX cluster is properly set up with the specified parameters and dependencies.

