### Description:
The Terraform program will create an AWS SageMaker Notebook Instance using the official HashiCorp Terraform AWS provider. The notebook instance will be configured to use a specific AMI and instance type, and it will be associated with an IAM role for authentication.

### Terraform HCL Program:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "ami_id" {
  description = "AMI ID for the SageMaker Notebook Instance"
  default     = "ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0"  # Example AMI ID for Amazon Linux 2
}

variable "instance_type" {
  description = "Instance type for the SageMaker Notebook Instance"
  default     = "ml.t2.medium"  # Example instance type
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "notebook_instance_role" {
  name = "sagemaker-notebook-instance-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "sagemaker.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "notebook_instance_policy_attachment" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonSageMakerFullAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.notebook_instance_role.name
}

resource "aws_sagemaker_notebook_instance" "example" {
  name           = "my-sagemaker-notebook"
  instance_type  = var.instance_type
  role_arn       = aws_iam_role.notebook_instance_role.arn
  subnet_id      = "subnet-12345678"  # Replace with your subnet ID
  security_groups = ["sg-12345678"]  # Replace with your security group ID

  tags = {
    Name = "MySageMakerNotebook"
  }

  lifecycle {
    create_before_destroy = true
  }
}
```

### Explanation:
- **Provider Configuration**: The `provider "aws"` block specifies the AWS region where the resources will be created.
- **Variables**: The `variable` blocks define the AMI ID and instance type for the notebook instance. Default values are provided for these variables.
- **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `sagemaker-notebook-instance-role` is created with permissions to assume the role of an Amazon SageMaker service.
- **IAM Policy Attachment**: The `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment` resource attaches the `AmazonSageMakerFullAccess` policy to the IAM role.
- **SageMaker Notebook Instance**: The `aws_sagemaker_notebook_instance` resource creates the notebook instance with the specified AMI ID, instance type, role ARN, subnet ID, and security groups. The `lifecycle { create_before_destroy = true }` block ensures that the notebook instance is recreated if it is destroyed and then recreated again.

Make sure to replace `"subnet-12345678"` and `"sg-12345678"` with your actual subnet and security group IDs.

