### Description:
The Terraform program will create a serverless Apache Kafka (MSK) cluster in the `us-east-2` region. The cluster will be configured with a single broker and will use the latest version of the MSK software. The program will also create an IAM role for the MSK cluster to allow it to access other AWS services.

### Terraform HCL Program:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-2"
}

variable "msk_cluster_name" {
  description = "Name of the MSK cluster"
  default     = "my-msk-cluster"
}

variable "msk_broker_type" {
  description = "Type of MSK broker"
  default     = "m5.large"
}

variable "msk_kafka_version" {
  description = "Version of Kafka to use"
  default     = "3.4.0"
}

resource "aws_msk_cluster" "example" {
  cluster_name = var.msk_cluster_name

  kafka_version = var.msk_kafka_version
  number_of_brokers = 1
  broker_node_group_info {
    instance_type = var.msk_broker_type
    instance_count = 1
    ebs_storage_info {
      volume_size = 20
    }
  }

  tags = {
    Name = var.msk_cluster_name
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "msk_cluster_role" {
  name = "${var.msk_cluster_name}-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "kafka.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "msk_cluster_policy_attachment" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonMQBrokerServiceRole"
  role       = aws_iam_role.msk_cluster_role.name
}
```

### Explanation:
- **Provider Configuration**: The `aws` provider is configured with the `us-east-2` region.
- **Variables**: 
  - `msk_cluster_name`: The name of the MSK cluster.
  - `msk_broker_type`: The type of MSK broker (e.g., `m5.large`).
  - `msk_kafka_version`: The version of Kafka to use (e.g., `3.4.0`).
- **Resource `aws_msk_cluster`**: This resource creates the MSK cluster with a single broker. It specifies the broker type, number of brokers, and EBS storage information.
- **Resource `aws_iam_role`**: This resource creates an IAM role named `${var.msk_cluster_name}-role` that allows the MSK cluster to assume the role.
- **Resource `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment`**: This resource attaches the `AmazonMQBrokerServiceRole` policy to the IAM role, granting the necessary permissions for the MSK cluster to interact with other AWS services.

