### Description of the Terraform Program

The Terraform program will create an AWS CodeBuild project to run students' code stored on GitHub. The project will use a specific environment and store the results. The program will also create necessary IAM roles and configure the CodeBuild project to access GitHub.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Create an IAM role for CodeBuild to assume
resource "aws_iam_role" "codebuild_role" {
  name = "codebuild-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "codebuild.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Attach policies to the IAM role
resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "codebuild_policy_attachment" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSCodeBuildServiceRolePolicy"
  role       = aws_iam_role.codebuild_role.name
}

# Create a CodeBuild project
resource "aws_codebuild_project" "autograder" {
  name         = "cs-class-autograder"
  description = "Autograder for CS class"

  source {
    type        = "GitHub"
    location   = "https://github.com/your-repo-url.git"
    git_clone_depth = 1
  }

  artifacts {
    type = "S3"
    location = "s3://your-bucket-name/autograder-results"
  }

  environment {
    compute_type = "BUILD_GENERAL1_SMALL"
    image        = "aws/codebuild/standard:4.0"
    privileged_mode = true
  }

  service_role = aws_iam_role.codebuild_role.arn
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The `provider "aws"` block specifies the AWS region where the infrastructure will be deployed.

2. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `codebuild-role` is created to allow CodeBuild to assume it. This role is attached to the `AWSCodeBuildServiceRolePolicy`, which provides the necessary permissions for CodeBuild to interact with AWS services.

3. **CodeBuild Project**: A CodeBuild project named `cs-class-autograder` is created. It uses GitHub as the source repository and stores the build artifacts in an S3 bucket. The project runs on a `BUILD_GENERAL1_SMALL` compute type using the `aws/codebuild/standard:4.0` image, which includes Python and other necessary tools. The `privileged_mode` is set to `true` to allow the use of Docker containers.

4. **Variables**: The `source.location` and `artifacts.location` fields are placeholders and should be replaced with the actual GitHub repository URL and S3 bucket name.

This Terraform program will create the necessary infrastructure to run students' code on GitHub and store the results in an S3 bucket.

