### Description of the Terraform Program

The Terraform program will create an AWS S3 bucket to store student code and the results of the autograder. It will also set up an AWS CodeBuild project to compile and run the student code in a specific environment. The program will use IAM roles to manage access to these resources.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

variable "github_repo_url" {
  description = "URL of the GitHub repository containing student code"
  default     = "https://github.com/example/cs-class-student-code.git"
}

variable "codebuild_image" {
  description = "Docker image to use for the CodeBuild project"
  default     = "amazonlinux:latest"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "student_code" {
  bucket = "cs-class-student-code-bucket"

  lifecycle {
    prevent_destroy = true
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_object" "student_code_zip" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.student_code.bucket
  key    = "student_code.zip"
  source = "path/to/student_code.zip"
}

resource "aws_codebuild_project" "autograder" {
  name          = "cs-class-autograder"
  description   = "Autograder for CS class"
  service_role  = aws_iam_role.autograder.arn
  source {
    type        = "GitHub"
    location    = var.github_repo_url
    git_clone_depth = 1
  }
  artifacts {
    type        = "zip"
    path        = "output"
    packaging   = "zip"
  }
  environment {
    compute_type = "BUILD_GENERAL1_SMALL"
    image        = var.codebuild_image
    privileged   = true
  }
  timeout_in_minutes = 60
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "autograder" {
  name = "cs-class-autograder-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "codebuild.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "autograder_policy" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.autograder.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSCodeBuildServiceRolePolicy"
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The `aws` provider is configured with the `region` set to `us-west-2`.

2. **Variables**: 
   - `github_repo_url`: The URL of the GitHub repository containing student code. The default value is set to `https://github.com/example/cs-class-student-code.git`.
   - `codebuild_image`: The Docker image to use for the CodeBuild project. The default value is set to `amazonlinux:latest`.

3. **S3 Bucket**:
   - `aws_s3_bucket.student_code`: Creates an S3 bucket named `cs-class-student-code-bucket`.
   - `aws_s3_bucket_object.student_code_zip`: Uploads the student code to the S3 bucket as a ZIP file.

4. **CodeBuild Project**:
   - `aws_codebuild_project.autograder`: Sets up a CodeBuild project named `cs-class-autograder`.
   - The project uses the `github` source type to pull the student code from the specified GitHub repository.
   - The project outputs the results to a ZIP file in the `output` directory.
   - The project runs in a `BUILD_GENERAL1_SMALL` compute type using the specified Docker image.
   - The project has a timeout of 60 minutes.

5. **IAM Role**:
   - `aws_iam_role.autograder`: Creates an IAM role named `cs-class-autograder-role`.
   - The role assumes the `AWSCodeBuildServiceRole` policy, which allows the CodeBuild service to assume the role.

6. **IAM Role Policy Attachment**:
   - `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment.autograder_policy`: Attaches the `AWSCodeBuildServiceRolePolicy` to the `cs-class-autograder-role`.

