### Description of the Terraform Program

The Terraform program will create an AWS CloudFront distribution to serve video content globally. It will use AWS S3 to store the video files. The program will also create IAM roles and policies to manage access to these resources.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "bucket_name" {
  description = "Name of the S3 bucket"
  default     = "video-streaming-bucket"
}

variable "cloudfront_domain_name" {
  description = "Domain name for the CloudFront distribution"
  default     = "example.com"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "video_bucket" {
  bucket = var.bucket_name
  acl    = "public-read"

  website {
    index_document = "index.html"
    error_document = "error.html"
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_policy" "video_bucket_policy" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.video_bucket.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Principal = "*"
        Action   = [
          "s3:GetObject",
          "s3:ListBucket"
        ]
        Resource = [
          "${aws_s3_bucket.video_bucket.arn}",
          "${aws_s3_bucket.video_bucket.arn}/*"
        ]
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_cloudfront_distribution" "video_distribution" {
  origin {
    domain_name = aws_s3_bucket.video_bucket.website_endpoint
    origin_id   = "S3Origin-${aws_s3_bucket.video_bucket.id}"
  }

  default_cache_behavior {
    allowed_methods   = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    cached_methods   = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    target_origin_id = "S3Origin-${aws_s3_bucket.video_bucket.id}"

    viewer_protocol_policy = "allow-all"
    min_ttl                = 0
    default_ttl              = 3600
    max_ttl                = 86400
  }

  enabled = true
  is_ipv6_enabled = true

  restrictions {
    geo_restriction {
      restriction_type = "whitelist"
      locations       = ["US", "CA", "UK", "DE"]
    }
  }

  custom_error_response {
    error_code           = 403
    response_page_path = "/error.html"
    response_code       = 200
  }

  logging_config {
    bucket = "s3-logs-${var.bucket_name}"
    prefix = "cloudfront-logs/"
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "Video Streaming Distribution"
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "cloudfront_access_role" {
  name = "CloudFrontAccessRole"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "cloudfront.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "cloudfront_access_policy" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.cloudfront_access_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess"
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The `aws` provider is configured to use the `us-east-1` region.

2. **Variables**: 
   - `bucket_name`: The name of the S3 bucket where video files will be stored.
   - `cloudfront_domain_name`: The domain name for the CloudFront distribution.

3. **S3 Bucket**:
   - An S3 bucket is created with the specified name and set to public read access.
   - A website configuration is added to enable static website hosting.

4. **S3 Bucket Policy**:
   - A policy is attached to the S3 bucket to allow public access to objects.

5. **CloudFront Distribution**:
   - A CloudFront distribution is created with an S3 origin.
   - Default cache behavior is set to allow GET and HEAD methods and to serve objects from the S3 bucket.
   - Restrictions are applied to restrict access to specific geographic locations.
   - Custom error responses are configured for 403 errors.
   - Logging is enabled to log requests to an S3 bucket.

6. **IAM Role**:
   - An IAM role is created for CloudFront to assume.
   - A policy is attached to the role to allow read access to S3.

This configuration ensures that the video streaming site can serve video content globally using AWS CloudFront and AWS S3, with appropriate security measures in place.

