### Description of the Terraform Program

The Terraform program will set up a video streaming site using AWS CloudFront, AWS Route53, and AWS S3. It will also include additional services such as AWS Lambda for content processing and AWS IAM roles for managing access.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

variable "domain_name" {
  description = "The domain name for the video streaming site."
  default     = "example.com"
}

variable "s3_bucket_name" {
  description = "The name of the S3 bucket to store video content."
  default     = "video-streaming-bucket"
}

variable "lambda_function_name" {
  description = "The name of the Lambda function for content processing."
  default     = "video-processing-function"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "video_streaming_bucket" {
  bucket = var.s3_bucket_name
  acl    = "private"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_policy" "video_streaming_bucket_policy" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.video_streaming_bucket.bucket

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Principal = "*"
        Action   = [
          "s3:GetObject",
          "s3:PutObject",
          "s3:DeleteObject"
        ]
        Resource = "arn:aws:s3:::${aws_s3_bucket.video_streaming_bucket.bucket}/*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_lambda_function" "video_processing_function" {
  filename      = "video-processing-function.zip"
  function_name = var.lambda_function_name
  role          = aws_iam_role.video_processing_function_role.arn
  handler       = "index.handler"
  runtime       = "python3.8"

  source_code_hash = filebase64sha256("video-processing-function.zip")

  environment = {
    variables = {
      BUCKET_NAME = aws_s3_bucket.video_streaming_bucket.bucket
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "video_processing_function_role" {
  name = "video-processing-function-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "lambda.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "video_processing_function_policy_attachment" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.video_processing_function_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole"
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "example_com" {
  name = var.domain_name
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "www" {
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.example_com.zone_id
  name    = "www"
  type    = "A"
  ttl     = 300

  alias {
    name    = aws_cloudfront_distribution.video_streaming_distribution.distribution_domain_name
    zone_id = aws_cloudfront_distribution.video_streaming_distribution.hosted_zone_id
    evaluate_target_health = true
  }
}

resource "aws_cloudfront_distribution" "video_streaming_distribution" {
  origin {
    domain_name = aws_s3_bucket.video_streaming_bucket.bucket_regional_domain_name
    origin_id   = "S3Origin-${aws_s3_bucket.video_streaming_bucket.id}"
  }

  default_cache_behavior {
    allowed_methods   = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    cached_methods   = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    target_origin_id = "S3Origin-${aws_s3_bucket.video_streaming_bucket.id}"

    viewer_protocol_policy = "allow-all"
    min_ttl               = 0
    default_ttl             = 3600
    max_ttl               = 86400
  }

  enabled = true
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The `aws` provider is configured to use the `us-east-1` region.

2. **Variables**: 
   - `domain_name`: The domain name for the video streaming site.
   - `s3_bucket_name`: The name of the S3 bucket to store video content.
   - `lambda_function_name`: The name of the Lambda function for content processing.

3. **S3 Bucket**: An S3 bucket is created to store video content. The bucket is set to private.

4. **S3 Bucket Policy**: A policy is attached to the S3 bucket to allow public read/write access.

5. **Lambda Function**: A Lambda function is created to process video content. The function is configured to use the S3 bucket for storage and is assumed to have the necessary permissions.

6. **IAM Role**: An IAM role is created for the Lambda function to assume and execute actions.

7. **Route53 Zone**: A Route53 zone is created for the domain name.

8. **Route53 Record**: A CNAME record is created to point the `www` subdomain to the CloudFront distribution.

9. **CloudFront Distribution**: A CloudFront distribution is created to serve the video content from the S3 bucket. The distribution is configured to allow public access and has a default cache behavior that allows GET and HEAD requests.

