### Description:
This Terraform program defines a load balancer using AWS Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) and associates it with Elastic IPs for public access. The load balancer will distribute incoming traffic across multiple instances or targets.

### Terraform HCL Program:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "elb_name" {
  description = "Name of the Elastic Load Balancer"
  default     = "my-elb"
}

variable "instance_ids" {
  description = "List of instance IDs to attach to the load balancer"
  type        = list(string)
  default     = []
}

variable "security_group_id" {
  description = "ID of the security group to apply to the load balancer"
  type        = string
  default     = ""
}

variable "subnets" {
  description = "List of subnet IDs where the load balancer will be placed"
  type        = list(string)
  default     = []
}

resource "aws_elb" "example" {
  name               = var.elb_name
  subnets            = var.subnets
  security_groups    = [var.security_group_id]
  listeners          = [
    {
      protocol           = "HTTP"
      load_balancer_port = 80
      instance_protocol  = "HTTP"
      instance_port      = 80
    }
  ]
  health_check {
    target             = "HTTP:80/"
    interval           = 30
    timeout            = 5
    healthy_threshold   = 2
    unhealthy_threshold = 2
  }
}

resource "aws_eip" "elb_eip" {
  count = length(var.instance_ids)

  vpc = true

  tags = {
    Name = "${var.elb_name}-eip-${count.index + 1}"
  }
}

resource "aws_elb_attachment" "example" {
  count = length(var.instance_ids)

  elb_id      = aws_elb.example.id
  instance_id = var.instance_ids[count.index]
  private_ip  = aws_eip.elb_eip[count.index].public_ip
}
```

### Explanation:
- **Provider Configuration**: The `aws` provider is configured with the desired AWS region (`us-west-2`).
- **Variables**: 
  - `elb_name`: The name of the Elastic Load Balancer.
  - `instance_ids`: A list of instance IDs to attach to the load balancer.
  - `security_group_id`: The ID of the security group to apply to the load balancer.
  - `subnets`: A list of subnet IDs where the load balancer will be placed.
- **Resources**:
  - `aws_elb`: Creates the Elastic Load Balancer with HTTP listener on port 80.
  - `aws_eip`: Creates Elastic IPs for each instance.
  - `aws_elb_attachment`: Attaches each instance to the load balancer using its private IP and the corresponding Elastic IP.

This configuration ensures that the load balancer is accessible via the internet and can route traffic to the specified instances.

