### Description:
This Terraform program defines a Load Balancer with an Authentication-OIDC action using AWS services. The Load Balancer will be configured to authenticate incoming requests using an OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider. This setup is useful for securing web applications by requiring users to authenticate before accessing them.

### Terraform HCL Program:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "load_balancer_name" {
  default = "my-load-balancer"
}

variable "security_group_id" {
  default = "sg-0abcdef1234567890"  # Replace with your existing security group ID
}

variable "vpc_id" {
  default = "vpc-0abcdef1234567890"  # Replace with your existing VPC ID
}

resource "aws_lb" "example" {
  name               = var.load_balancer_name
  internal           = false
  subnets            = [var.vpc_id]
  security_groups     = [var.security_group_id]
  enable_deletion_protection = true

  listener {
    protocol      = "HTTP"
    port          = 80
    default_action {
      type             = "authenticate_oidc"
      authenticate_oidc_config {
        authorization_endpoint = "https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth"
        client_id             = "your-client-id"
        client_secret         = "your-client-secret"
        issuer                = "https://accounts.google.com"
        token_endpoint        = "https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/token"
        user_info_endpoint    = "https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v3/userinfo"
        authentication_request_extra_params = {
          scope = "openid email profile"
        }
        on_unauthenticated_request = "deny"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Explanation:

1. **Provider Configuration**: The `provider "aws"` block specifies the AWS region where the resources will be created. Replace `"us-west-2"` with your desired region.

2. **Variables**: 
   - `load_balancer_name`: The name of the load balancer.
   - `security_group_id`: The ID of the security group associated with the load balancer.
   - `vpc_id`: The ID of the VPC where the load balancer will be deployed.

3. **Load Balancer Resource**:
   - `aws_lb "example"` creates a load balancer with the specified name, internal flag, subnets, security groups, and deletion protection.
   - A listener is added to the load balancer on port 80, which uses the `authenticate_oidc` action.

4. **Authenticate-OIDC Configuration**:
   - `authenticate_oidc_config` specifies the OIDC provider details such as the authorization endpoint, client ID, client secret, issuer, token endpoint, user info endpoint, and additional parameters.
   - `on_unauthenticated_request` is set to `"deny"`, meaning unauthenticated requests will be denied.

### Notes:
- Ensure you replace placeholders like `"your-client-id"` and `"your-client-secret"` with your actual Google OAuth 2.0 client ID and secret.
- The `issuer` should match the domain of your OIDC provider.
- This configuration assumes you have a Google account and have set up an OIDC provider for your application.

