### Description:
This Terraform program creates an Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) with a lifecycle policy that automatically transitions files to the Infrequent Access (IA) storage class after a certain period of inactivity. The lifecycle policy ensures that data is stored efficiently based on usage patterns.

### Terraform HCL Program:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "efs_name" {
  description = "Name of the EFS file system"
  default     = "my-efs"
}

variable "lifecycle_policy" {
  description = "Lifecycle policy for EFS files"
  default     = <<EOF
{
  "Rules": [
    {
      "ID": "TransitionToIA",
      "Status": "ENABLED",
      "Transitions": [
        {
          "TimeInDays": 30,
          "StorageClass": "STANDARD_IA"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
EOF
}

resource "aws_efs_file_system" "example" {
  name = var.efs_name

  tags = {
    Name = var.efs_name
  }
}

resource "aws_efs_lifecycle_policy" "example" {
  file_system_id = aws_efs_file_system.example.id
  lifecycle_policy = jsonencode(var.lifecycle_policy)
}
```

### Explanation:
- **Provider Configuration**: The `aws` provider is configured with the desired AWS region (`us-west-2`).
- **Variables**:
  - `efs_name`: Specifies the name of the EFS file system. Default is `my-efs`.
  - `lifecycle_policy`: Defines the lifecycle policy for the EFS files. The default policy transitions files to the IA storage class after 30 days.
- **Resources**:
  - `aws_efs_file_system`: Creates the EFS file system with the specified name and tags.
  - `aws_efs_lifecycle_policy`: Applies the lifecycle policy to the EFS file system.

This configuration is deployable with Terraform version ~> 1.9.8 and requires the `hashicorp/aws` provider version ~> 5.75. Make sure to replace `"us-west-2"` with your desired AWS region.

